1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,934
AI video generators now produce minutes of
footage from a single prompt.

2
00:00:05,994 --> 00:00:07,799
They also fail quietly.

3
00:00:07,859 --> 00:00:10,596
A prop changes design between shots.

4
00:00:10,656 --> 00:00:13,859
A line of dialogue comes out wrong.

5
00:00:13,919 --> 00:00:18,987
Nobody notices until a human scrubs every
second of every render.

6
00:00:19,047 --> 00:00:24,582
And asking a second model, "does this look
fine?", is not evidence.

7
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:31,222
ProofFrame is an independent verification
layer that sits between the approved brief

8
00:00:31,282 --> 00:00:32,767
and the generator.

9
00:00:32,827 --> 00:00:33,797
Three rules.

10
00:00:33,857 --> 00:00:35,343
One: blind observation.

11
00:00:35,403 --> 00:00:41,009
The checking model never sees the expected
answer while it watches.

12
00:00:41,069 --> 00:00:42,039
Two: fail-closed.

13
00:00:42,099 --> 00:00:48,221
If a check cannot be verified, it is
unresolved, never a pass.

14
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:54,402
Three: every finding is tied to frames and
timestamps, so a human,

15
00:00:54,462 --> 00:00:58,523
or the generator, can act on it immediately.

16
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,353
Give ProofFrame the film and its contract,

17
00:01:02,413 --> 00:01:05,767
the locked script compiled into checkable
assertions,

18
00:01:05,827 --> 00:01:08,692
and it verifies shot by shot.

19
00:01:08,752 --> 00:01:11,130
This handle must stay folded.

20
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:12,106
It doesn't.

21
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:14,544
This lantern must not change.

22
00:01:14,604 --> 00:01:15,519
It does.

23
00:01:15,579 --> 00:01:20,883
Dialogue is checked too, by two independent
transcribers: Muse Voice Transcribe,

24
00:01:20,943 --> 00:01:26,734
and ElevenLabs Scribe, which we use because
it handles Vietnamese dialogue better.

25
00:01:26,794 --> 00:01:28,685
Neither sees the script.

26
00:01:28,745 --> 00:01:30,148
When they disagree,

27
00:01:30,208 --> 00:01:35,024
the line is flagged with exactly what each
one heard.

28
00:01:35,084 --> 00:01:38,925
This full-episode contract run cost eight
dollars thirty.

29
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:42,635
And here is the whole thing, live.

30
00:01:42,695 --> 00:01:46,572
We upload a one-minute excerpt with a
four-check contract,

31
00:01:46,632 --> 00:01:48,321
and start the run.

32
00:01:48,381 --> 00:01:51,821
Nothing is staged: this page is the product,

33
00:01:51,881 --> 00:01:54,008
polling as the checks complete.

34
00:01:54,068 --> 00:01:57,944
Two minutes later the verdict is in —
blocked.

35
00:01:58,004 --> 00:02:02,756
The carrying-handle check failed, and the
continuity audit failed with it.

36
00:02:02,816 --> 00:02:05,380
The whole run cost sixty-four cents.

37
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:09,755
Click a finding, and the evidence opens: the
frames checked,

38
00:02:09,815 --> 00:02:11,942
the seconds they came from.

39
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:17,489
Findings are structured, so they feed
straight back to production.

40
00:02:17,549 --> 00:02:22,504
This line lost its first word at an edit
boundary.

41
00:02:22,564 --> 00:02:24,510
Both transcribers confirmed it.

42
00:02:24,570 --> 00:02:30,529
Production fixed the trim, we re-ran, and
the same check now passes.

43
00:02:30,589 --> 00:02:36,547
Fix exactly what is flagged, re-run, and the
result is classified: fixed,

44
00:02:36,607 --> 00:02:38,554
still failing, or regressed.

45
00:02:38,614 --> 00:02:40,058
No full re-watch.

46
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:44,346
Built solo during the hackathon on Muse
Spark,

47
00:02:44,406 --> 00:02:49,672
through the Meta Model API, with ElevenLabs
Scribe for dialogue transcription.

48
00:02:49,732 --> 00:02:55,481
It is being tested on a Vietnamese
AI-generated school-mystery series — and

49
00:02:55,541 --> 00:02:59,838
every clip in this video comes from that
work.
